# This CITATION.cff makes the software citable (e.g. via GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" button and Zenodo DOI minting). APA/BibTeX exports below.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'IELTS-API: A Free, No-Auth, Open IELTS Practice API in TypeScript'
message: 'If you use IELTS-API in research or teaching, please cite it as below.'
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API'
url: 'https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API'
abstract: >-
  IELTS-API is a free, no-authentication REST API and open dataset for IELTS
  (International English Language Testing System) preparation. It serves
  CEFR-graded vocabulary, Writing Task 1/2 prompts with band-scored samples,
  Speaking Parts 1-3 topics, Reading/Listening question taxonomies and practice
  sets, grammar rules, academic collocations, idioms, phrasal verbs, study
  plans, and deterministic band-score calculators. Implemented in TypeScript
  with 100% test coverage.
keywords:
  - ielts
  - english-language-assessment
  - esl
  - efl
  - computer-assisted-language-learning
  - open-educational-resources
  - rest-api
  - typescript
authors:
  - family-names: 'IELTS-API contributors'
    name: 'IELTS-API contributors'
